{\b\fs22 MAD Toolbox Privacy Policy}\par\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab We collect and upload nothing: no accounts, no telemetry, no crash reporting.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Your sign-in credentials, task history and downloads stay on your device only.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Downloads happen directly between you and the platform \u8212? traffic never passes through our servers.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Checking for updates contacts our version server; that is our only data channel, and it carries none of your personal data.\par\pard
\par
{\b\fs20 Introduction}\par
This Privacy Policy explains how MAD Toolbox handles information. It applies to this website and to the MAD Toolbox application, whatever the distribution channel, including versions installed through the Microsoft Store. The party responsible under this policy is MAD Producer Studio (\u8220?we\u8221?, \u8220?us\u8221?).\par
MAD Toolbox is built on a local-first, minimum-collection principle: the app does all of its work on your device, and we operate no servers that gather user data. Please read this policy to understand what stays on your device, which network requests occur, and how responsibility is divided between us and third-party platforms.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Information we do not collect}\par
We do not collect, record or upload any personally identifiable information. Specifically:\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab This website uses no tracking cookies and no analytics services. Your language preference is saved only in your browser's localStorage, so the site can remember your interface language.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab The app has no account system and never asks you to register for or sign in to any service of ours.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab The app contains no telemetry: we do not collect usage behaviour, device information or performance data.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab The app contains no crash reporting: crash information is never sent to us or to any third party.\par\pard
We build no user profiles and we do not track you across devices or services.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Data stored on your device}\par
Everything the app works with stays on your device, including:\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Task records and task logs;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Preferences and application state;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Bilibili credentials obtained through QR-code sign-in (cookies such as SESSDATA);\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Cookie files you import manually;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Media files you download (saved by default to the Downloads/MADToolbox folder in your system download directory; you can change the location).\par\pard
None of this data exists on our servers, and we keep no copies of it. Uninstalling the app or clearing its data deletes it for good. When you export a task log, the app redacts credential fields (such as SESSDATA and bili_jct) automatically, but you should always inspect a log before sharing it.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Network requests}\par
The app does not send your data to us. To complete a task you initiate, the app \u8212? together with the open-source tools it invokes, such as BBDown, yt-dlp and musicdl \u8212? communicates directly with the third-party platform you target, for example Bilibili, YouTube and other sites supported by yt-dlp, or the music platforms. That traffic does not pass through our servers, and we cannot see it.\par
When the app starts it checks for updates by fetching a version manifest from our distribution service at openlist.frameneo.com (cached by FRAMENEO's CDN). The request itself carries none of your personal data. The CDN provider records standard network logs \u8212? such as IP addresses \u8212? in line with industry practice, for security and service-quality purposes.\par
When the app is installed through the Microsoft Store, data processing tied to the store itself \u8212? download, update and licence verification \u8212? is governed by the Microsoft Privacy Statement (https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement) and is Microsoft's responsibility.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Third-party services and responsibility}\par
MAD Toolbox is a graphical front-end for independent open-source tools, including BBDown, yt-dlp, FFmpeg, MediaInfo, Deno and musicdl. Each tool runs under its own licence; see the third-party notices (https://github.com/MAD-Producer/MAD-Toolbox/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md) included with the application.\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Content, accounts and terms of service on each platform are defined and enforced by that platform. Whether and what you may download depends on the platform's rules and on your own account permissions.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Credentials you provide \u8212? QR-code sign-in or imported cookie files \u8212? are used only to authenticate you to the corresponding platform. They are never used for any other purpose and are never sent anywhere other than that platform.\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab We are not responsible for the availability of third-party platforms, for their content, or for any action a platform takes with regard to your account.\par\pard
Depending on which package you install (Full or Lite), some tools ship bundled with the app while others are installed by you through system package managers such as WinGet or Homebrew. musicdl is always installed separately and is never distributed with the app. Requests made while installing such dependencies go to the respective package repositories, not to us.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Copyright and tool neutrality}\par
MAD Toolbox does not provide, host, index or recommend any audio or video content. It has no content library and no catalogue: download targets are determined entirely by the links or IDs you enter. In this respect the app is a neutral, general-purpose channel, no different from a web browser or a download manager.\par
We expressly require that, when using the app, you:\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab fetch only content you are authorised to access;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab comply with each platform's terms of service and with the copyright law of your jurisdiction;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab use downloaded material solely for personal study and creative work;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab never redistribute, share or sell unauthorised material.\par\pard
The music feature depends on musicdl, which is licensed for non-commercial use and is not distributed with the app; the relevant licence terms and compliance requirements are stated in the app's dependency installation notes.\par
MAD Toolbox is fully open source, so anyone can audit its code and network behaviour. If you are a rights holder and believe that content infringes your rights: because we store no content, please direct your claim to the platform that actually hosts it. You may also contact us, and we will cooperate where reasonably possible.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Data security}\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab All user data stays local \u8212? there is no remote storage to breach;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab This website is served over HTTPS;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab In-app update packages are verified against a minisign public key, and installation is refused on signature mismatch;\par\pard
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab Release artifacts ship with a SHA256SUMS.txt file so you can verify their integrity yourself.\par\pard
If you discover a security issue, please contact us through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting (see Contact us) instead of disclosing credentials or exploit details in a public issue.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Children's privacy}\par
MAD Toolbox is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children. Because the app collects no data at all, children cannot provide personal information to us through it. If you believe personal information from a child has reached us in some other way, contact us and we will delete it promptly.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Changes to this policy}\par
If we change this policy, we will publish the change on this page and update the effective date at the top. Significant changes may also be announced on the website or in the app. Continuing to use the website or the app after a change takes effect means you accept the updated policy.\par
\par
{\b\fs20 Contact us}\par
For any question, request or complaint about this policy or our privacy practices, reach us on GitHub:\par
\pard\fi-180\li360\bullet\tab GitHub Issues: github.com/MAD-Producer/MAD-Toolbox/issues (https://github.com/MAD-Producer/MAD-Toolbox/issues)\par\pard
For security matters, please use GitHub's private vulnerability reporting rather than a public issue. We will never ask you for credentials or personal information outside these channels \u8212? beware of phishing attempts impersonating us.\par
\par}
